WEBVTT

1
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Nathan B.: Morning. Emma, the email numbers?

2
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Emma C.: The first week is in.

3
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Emma C.: First numbers after the email rewrite: calendar connects went from 72% to 79% in one week, on 118 signups.

4
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.000
Nathan B.: That's a big jump.

5
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.000
Emma C.: It is. I'd like to send it to everyone.

6
00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.000
Emma C.: Every week we wait costs us signups.

7
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:07.000
Nathan B.: Seven points in a week is a strong signal, but 118 signups is easy to misread.

8
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.000
Emma C.: So what do you suggest?

9
00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.000
Nathan B.: Keep testing, but on more people.

10
00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.000
Emma C.: Then let's at least widen the test.

11
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:25.000
Nathan B.: A hundred and eighteen signups is too few to bet everyone on.

12
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:45.000
Nathan B.: So let's not send it to everyone at once, half first.

13
00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:55.000
Emma C.: Half of new signups, then.

14
00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:12.000
Nathan B.: Yes, and we compare after two weeks.

15
00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:37.000
Emma C.: Fine: the new email two goes to an A/B test on 50% of signups.

16
00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:46.000
Nathan B.: Good. Log it on the email ticket.

17
00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.000
Emma C.: Will do.

18
00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.000
Nathan B.: And the checklist?

19
00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:53.000
Emma C.: Daniel finished it last week.

20
00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:17.000
Emma C.: Daniel's checklist went live for 20% of users on Monday; too early to read.

21
00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:26.000
Nathan B.: Let's read it in two weeks too.

22
00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:37.000
Emma C.: Same review, then.

23
00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:14.000
Emma C.: When do we decide on sending it to everyone?

24
00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.000
Nathan B.: Not before we have enough signups.

25
00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:57.000
Nathan B.: We decide on a 100% rollout after two weeks of data, not before.

26
00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:00.000
Emma C.: Two weeks, agreed.

27
00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:12.000
Nathan B.: Good.

28
00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:54.000
Nathan B.: How do we know the checklist helps?

29
00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:12.000
Emma C.: Bookings, not clicks.

30
00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:38.000
Emma C.: I'll watch the share of clinics without a first booking after the checklist, for two weeks.

31
00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:44.000
Nathan B.: Good. Thanks, Emma.

32
00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:52.000
Emma C.: Thanks.
